Z||000002||84Bill||05-18-2001||01:09 PM||||There is a guy I know of that does perfect chrome work I mean perfect! It will take him a while to do it and cost a bit more but the man is a craftsman and won't mess it up at all. LMK if you want more info.||||reg||14
Z||000003||p4n1c||05-18-2001||01:24 PM||||They are the badging for my Cutlass.  All of the badging minus the international symbols are chromed plastic(I think it's plastic).  And the trim on the bottom of the brake lights.<P>Is there a special paint or something to do this?  I figured I would ask here, because I though the Pontiac on some of the coupe's were chrome.<P>Thanks again  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4 OD auto<BR>"Ride the geriatric mobile.. err..  rocket"||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||05-18-2001||05:04 PM||||There is a special process for making a chrome 'like' coating. Its hard to find someone who does it. Might try finding someone in your area that makes the 'gold' lettering, theyd prob know someone. Its not real chrome, its the same process thats used in model cars to make bumpers, etc. The orig chrome plastic emblems arent very expensive from a dealer, sometimes only a few dollars each.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Pontiaddict||05-19-2001||08:40 PM||||Well, you could go to a hobby shop and buy some chrome leaf matereal (not sure on the name) and do it yourself if you want to. Or you could do some custom painting to the emblems for a unique look.||||reg||1
Z||000006||cadaver||05-19-2001||10:04 PM||||I have plastic chromed all the time. And yes it is real chrome. Dont know about the factory stuff but the stuff I have done is.||||reg||1
Z||000007||gabriel||05-21-2001||04:29 PM||||You can chrome plate plastic - or anything else for that matter - there is a process that precoats the non metal material & allows for real chrome plating. Jewlers use it for gold plating little things. Its a 24 carat plating with a small amount of boron added for hardness.  It's knd of labor intensive so it costs.  I was thinking about starting that service myself for dashboards and such if there is any demand, but as I wrote, it's not cheap.  As far as emblems go, they would have to be pen or brush stick chrome plated ...  again, $$$$$.<P>  Roger is right about the Gold plating services - they can do it themselves with chrome (or black chrome) if they are set up with the correct (incredibly expensive) chemicals & tools.||||reg||1
